-- title:
--   Fifteen-step Syracuse descent on chunk 1 of the modulus-$2^{24}$ refinement (2423 residue classes)
-- statement:
--   Let $T(n)$ be the odd part of $3n+1$ (the platform's Syracuse map `syracuseStep`), and let $T^{15}$ denote fifteen successive applications. Let $R_1$ be the explicit list of 2423 distinct residues modulo $2^{24}=16777216$ enumerated in the formal statement. For every natural number $n$,
--
--   $$
--   n\bmod 16777216\in R_{1}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad T^{15}(n)<n.
--   $$
--
--   This is chunk 1 of 4 of the modulus-$2^{24}$ refinement of the [twentyseven-branch residual after the modulus-$2^{23}$ refinement](https://prove2.me/theorems/d18594d3-5673-4cdc-acfb-51f35c5e2df0); the four chunks are disjoint and together cover 9690 residue classes, all lying over the leaf's 30485 surviving classes modulo $2^{23}$ and each admitting a descent certificate with exponent budget $24$. Every listed residue satisfies $r\equiv 27\pmod{32}$ and avoids all earlier exclusion lists.
--
--   **Method.** For each $r\in R_1$ the first fourteen Syracuse steps of $r$ are exact rows $3b_i+1=2^{a_i}b_{i+1}$ with $b_0=r$ and odd $b_{i+1}$, with $S=\sum_{i<14}a_i\le 24$, and the fifteenth row is closed by a divisor exponent $e=\min(v_2(3b_{14}+1),\,24-S)$ with quotient $B=(3b_{14}+1)/2^{e}<r$. The published theorem [`CollatzFrontier.syracuse_terminal_budget_of_descent`](https://prove2.me/theorems/2513a4d3-77eb-4b93-9876-33755812122c) then gives $T^{15}(r+2^{24}q)<r+2^{24}q$ for all $q$. The chunk is checked by one kernel evaluation of the checker over its literal list, so the 9690-class refinement is split into four independently checked theorems.
--
--   **Role.** Together with the other three chunks and the refined residual `syracuse_descent_residual_twentyseven_mod32_mod2097152_after_step15_mod16777216` it reduces the open frontier leaf [`syracuse_descent_residual_twentyseven_mod32_mod2097152_after_step14_mod8388608`](https://prove2.me/theorems/d18594d3-5673-4cdc-acfb-51f35c5e2df0) by a case split on membership in the four chunk lists; the four chunks together remove $9690/60970\approx 15.9\%$ of the leaf's open classes without bounding the starting value or the descent time.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The map is the existing definition `syracuseStep`; the residue list is a literal `List ℕ` inside the theorem's type, as in the earlier list theorems of this branch. The recursion-depth option only supports elaboration of the long literal. No monotonicity of the Syracuse map is asserted.
